WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.822
This query first subtracts admit time from discharge time.

00:00:03.822 --> 00:00:05.647
That produces an interval.

00:00:05.647 --> 00:00:12.317
It also converts the interval to seconds using EXTRACT EPOCH, divides by the number of seconds in a

00:00:12.317 --> 00:00:14.022
day, and rounds the result.

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:16.452
The interval is a typed duration.

00:00:16.452 --> 00:00:21.737
The numeric day value is an analytical representation derived from that duration.

00:00:21.737 --> 00:00:26.092
Text cleaning should separate normalization from interpretation.

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:31.872
Trimming spaces or standardizing case is usually safe when the rule is documented;

00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:37.817
correcting a person's name or guessing an email address is a much stronger intervention.

00:00:37.817 --> 00:00:41.194
Preserve the original value when auditability matters.
